esponse to GLP-1 (By similarity).ACTIVITY REGULATION The allosteric modulators NNC0640, PF-06372222 and MK-0893 inhibit the increase of intracellular cAMP levels in response to GLP-1.SUBUNIT May form homodimers and heterodimers with GIPR.INTERACTION N-glycosylation enhances cell surface expression and lengthens receptor half-life by preventing degradation in the ER.MISCELLANEOUS Selective recognition of glucagon-like peptide over glucagon is determined by residues located at the C-terminal end of the glucagon-like peptide.SIMILARITY Belongs to the G-protein coupled receptor 2 family.ONLINE INFORMATION Glucagon-like peptide 1 entry"],"description":["recommendedName: Glucagon-like peptide 1 receptor shortName: GLP-1 receptor shortName: GLP-1-R shortName: GLP-1R"],"geneName":["GLP1R"],"isSequenceChanged":false,"keyword":["3D-structure","ADP-ribosylation","Cell membrane","Disulfide bond","G-protein coupled receptor","Glycoprotein","Membrane","Receptor","Reference proteome","Signal","Transducer","Transmembrane","Transmembrane helix"],"secondaryIdentifier":["GLP1R_HUMAN","Q2M229","Q99669"],"sequenceLength":463,"species":48887,"chain":["signal peptide:1-23","chain:24-463"],"referenceGene":[{"dbId":8996587,"displayName":"ENSEMBL:ENSG00000112164 GLP1R","stId":"ensembl:ENSG00000112164","databaseName":"ENSEMBL","identifier":"ENSG00000112164","url":"https://www.ensembl.org/id/ENSG00000112164","moleculeType":"Entity","geneName":["GLP1R"],"className":"ReferenceDNASequence","schemaClass":"ReferenceDNASequence"},{"dbId":12734191,"displayName":"UCSC:P43220 GLP1R","databaseName":"UCSC","identifier":"P43220","url":"https://genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgLinkIn?id=P43220&resource=uniprot","moleculeType":"Entity","geneName":["GLP1R"],"className":"ReferenceDNASequence","schemaClass":"ReferenceDNASequence"},{"dbId":11354356,"displayName":"BioGPS Gene:2740 GLP1R","databaseName":"BioGPS Gene","identifier":"2740","url":"https://biogps.org/gene/2740","moleculeType":"Entity","geneName":["GLP1R"],"c